From cc8e1a0abd86cdc440ec636593d1bc5bc931c76f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thiagu <thiagu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 04:54:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add Home nav icon, drop redundant back arrow, add
 logo/favicon upload
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- NavMenu: add a Home icon link ahead of the admin-configured page
  links (About/Products/...), calling onNavigate("home") — App.jsx
  already treats "home" as a valid page id, no routing changes needed.
- Remove the back-arrow (BackButton) shown next to the logo on the
  chat/content/contact pages — now redundant with the Home nav icon
  and the logo's own click-to-home behavior.
- Admin Branding settings: image-typed fields (logo_url, favicon_url)
  now offer a file-upload button alongside the existing URL text
  input, wired to the existing POST /admin/api/uploads/image endpoint
  (adminApi.uploadImage). Includes a small preview thumbnail.

Frontend (root) and admin builds both pass; backend test suite (137
tests) unaffected by these frontend-only changes.
